{
  "request": {
    "model": "nomic-embed-text:latest",
    "input": [
      "Synthetic nurse note for software testing. No real patient data.\n\nAt a scheduled commercial-driver medical, the driver answers questions in several stages because a dispatcher keeps calling about the next route, while the nurse checks a current clinical document against a copied workplace summary; an observation described confidently in conversation is kept separate from a finding actually recorded in an identified examination.\n\nThe driver sometimes notices vehicles late on the left and brings a field printout marked 140 degrees, but its reliability flag is poor and the treating optometrist has not confirmed a defect or a valid horizontal extent; central letters seem clear to the driver, no complete specialist interpretation is attached, and the nurse records the symptoms and the unreliable test separately rather than converting either into a confirmed static visual field disorder.\n\nThe employer's copied form relates to an earlier period of work and contains a broad satisfactory box without the measurements underlying it, whereas the current nurse entry identifies the source of each specific finding; the driver's wish to continue scheduled duties is recorded as a preference, not as proof that the present assessment has resolved the documented concern.\n\nThe nurse reads the summary back to the driver to check the chronology and separates agreement about the wording from verification of a medical finding, then attaches the identified clinical material; any decision about further investigation or work allocation remains for the reviewing professional, and the note itself does not certify that all relevant clinical questions have been answered.\n"
    ],
    "truncate": false
  },
  "provider_called": true,
  "status": "completed",
